KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ cerr good: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ cerr precision: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ cerr unitbuf: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ cerr tied to cout: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Meaningful only with the MSVC STL (Windows); elsewhere the #error makes it
fail.  provide_standard_stream_objects does not define the stream objects
for the MSVC STL: constructing a stream there initializes its locale
through runtime functions without a model (std::_Locinfo::_Locinfo_ctor,
_Getctype, _Getcvt, _Mbrtowc), so cout and cerr stay nondeterministic and
every assertion fails.  Checked with MSVC 14.51 headers preprocessed by cl.
